{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And its meal-offering: two tenths.</b> Double its meal-offering, because it is the offering at the beginning of the harvest — a sign of blessing for the produce, that it be blessed. And since its meal-offering is doubled, unlike the rest of the lambs, we mention in the Musaf prayer of the Festival the division of the tenths. And some say: one of these two tenths is the omer, which is a tenth, and it comes with this lamb; and the second tenth is the tenth fitting for its meal-offering. And their proof is that it does not add in the libation except a quarter of the hin, like the rest of the lambs. But this is nothing, for these two tenths come as wheat, since it is written of them סולת, and it is established to us that there is no סולת except from wheat, whereas the omer comes from barley." "<b>And its libation: a quarter of the hin of wine.</b> Rabbi Elazar said: it is written ונסכה, and we read ונסכו. How so? The libation of the meal-offering is like the libation of the wine: just as the libation of the wine is a quarter, so too the libation of the meal-offering — which is oil — meaning that there is nothing doubled in it except the meal-offering." "<b>And its meal-offering: two tenths.</b> And its libation of wine — because this offering is not destined to be written in the section of Pinchas, he wrote for you here 'and its meal-offering and its libation.' And likewise the seven lambs and one bull and two rams that come on Atzeret — because of the bread he mentioned them here with their meal-offerings and their libations, since they are not destined to be written in the section of Pinchas. But the rest of the offerings of the festivals are mentioned here generically, in the expression אשה, since they are destined — and their meal-offerings and their libations are destined — to be written in the section of Pinchas."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:37.550537024Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}